# Execute once; allegation format is fixed

## User instruction discipline

- When the user asks for a change, **implement it fully end-to-end** (backend emit + stored payloads + UI display) in the same turn.
- Do **not** leave the fix only in drafting code while the Compare/Report UI still shows stale quoted text.
- Do **not** ask the user to regenerate or restart unless you have already restarted the API yourself and verified the live path.
- Never make the user ask a second time for the same change unless completing it would destroy the build.

## Allegation line format (non-negotiable)

Baseline IR allegation shape — **no quotation marks** around duty phrases:

```
Potential violation of WAC {code}, {title}, by having failed to (label) duty; and (label) duty.
```

- Opener is `Potential violation` (not `A potential violation`).
- Strip ASCII and curly double quotes (`" “ ” „`) from every allegation string on draft, API emit, report rebuild, and frontend display/load (`normalize_allegation_line` / `normalizeAllegationLine`).
- Full statute quotes belong in Regulatory Framework / verification panels — **not** wrapped in the allegation line.
